 Figures 2A, B 
 ), which are major components of the glycocalyx. In line with the FD patient-derived data, treatment of EA.hy926-KO cells with recombinant AGAL (20 mg/ml) increased L-fucose and GlcNAc on AGAL-deficient cells by 8.0% and 10.0%, respectively (both p<0.001,  
 Figure 2B 
 ). An important process for glycocalyx degradation is the expression and release of heparanases due to an inflammatory stimulus.
